  "title": "Differential Equations Review",
  "body": " Differential Equations Review     The differential equation describes the height of an object suspended by a spring. Which of the following functions are solutions of this equation?                   The velocity of a falling object is described by the differential equation Which of the following functions are solutions of this equation?                 For what velocities does the velocity increase? For what velocities does the velocity decrease?      Sketch a slope field for this differential equation.      Identify any equilibrium solutions and determine whether they are stable or unstable.      What does this equilibrium solution mean in terms of the falling object?      Suppose that is measured in meters per second and is measured in seconds. Let's develop a numerical approximation of the solution that has an initial value of . What is the rate of change at this time? What are the units on this rate of change?      If we take time steps of seconds, by approximately how much does the velocity change from to ?      What is the estimate velocity when ?      Repeat this process to continue estimating the velocity (remember that this is called Euler's method and pronounced ``Oiler's method'')  \\begin{tabular}{c|c|c|c} & & & \\hline 0 & 0 & \\bm\\bm & \\bm\\bm \\bm0.1 &&& \\bm0.2 &\\bm\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm \\bm0.3 &\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm \\bm0.4 &\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm&\\bm\\bm \\end{tabular}  Verify that is the solution to the initial value problem given by this differential equation and the initial condition .      Compare your estimate of to the exact value of .        Convert the following statements into differential equations.  \\begin{itemize} \\item ``The rate of change of the balance of the account equals 6% of the balance.'' Write this as a differential equation for the balance .      \\item ``The population of a town is decreasing at the rate of 2% per year.'' Write this as a differential equation for the population .      \\item ``You have a mortgage that grows by 5% every year at the same time that you are decreasing it by paying $10,000 per year.'' Write this as a differential equation for , the balance of the mortgage. \\end{itemize}     "
