  "body": " Final Review     The probability density function describes the amount of time, in minutes, you wait to talk to a representative when you call your bank.  Find the cumulative distribution function. What does this function tell us?      Find the median waiting time.      Find the average waiting time.      What percentage of people wait less time than the average?      What percentage of people wait less time than the median?        Students are given a three-hour test and you record the length of time it takes students to complete the test. The cumulative distribution is given by  What is the median time it takes for students to complete the test?      If you finish in 2 hours, what percentage of students have finished before you?      What is the probability density function ?      The first quartile is the time at which 25% of students have finished the exam, and the third quartile is when 75% have. Find these times.      Find the average time it takes for students to finish the exam.        Consider the differential equation  Sketch a slope field for this equation and identify any equilbrium solutions. For each equilbrium, determine whether it is stable or unstable.      If , use Euler's method with a step size of 0.1 to estimate the value .        Find the solution to the following initial value problems.           "
